10151.text:
10151 mukta 'set free' MBh., °aka - 'separate' BhP. [~ * mukna-. — √muc ] Pa. mutta -, °aka - 'released', Dhp. muto , NiDoc. mutaṁti 3 pl. pret., Pk. mutta -, motta -; Dm. múta m., muti f. 'yearling kid' (i.e. 'independent of dam' NTS
xii 179); Tir. mvtəris karə 'let it loose' AO xii 184;
Phal. muto , mutto 'rain' NOPhal 43 (cf. Bshk. muč - 'a
cloud to open' < mucyátē ); Sh. mŭˊtŭs 1 sg. pret. of mŭčóĭki̯ 'to escape' < múcyatē , mŭtŭ 'other', (Lor.) mūto 'leavings'; K. mŏtᵘ pp. of mŏċun 'to remain over';
L. muttā pp. of muñjaṇ 'to send' < muñcáti , (Ju.) muttaṇ 'to send'; — Si. kam-mutu 'finished' ( kam - < kárman -¹?).

5599.text:
5599 * ḍhēra ¹ 'lump, heap'. 2. * dhēra- . [See list of words for 'lump' with initial ḍh - ( dh -) s.v. * ḍhikka -¹] 1. Paš. ḍēr 'heap'; K. ḍēr m. 'heap, store, granary';
S. ḍheru m. 'heap'; L. ḍher 'much, many', ḍherī f.
'hillock', mult. 'heap'; P. WPah.bhal. ḍher m. ' heap';
Ku. ḍher 'heap, large quantity', ḍheri f. 'heap'; N. ḍher , °ri 'heap, mass, bundle'; A. ḍher 'much', ḍheriba 'to
heap up', ḍerhi 'surplus, excess'; B. ḍhera 'much', ḍheri 'heap'; Or. ḍhera 'much'; Bi. ḍhērī 'heap (of grain
or manure)'; Mth. ḍher , °rī 'heap, quantity, much';
Aw. lakh. ḍhēr 'heap, many'; H. ḍher m., ḍherī f. 'heap',
G. ḍher m.; M. ḍher m. 'large lump', ḍherī f. 'little
heap'. 2. N. dher , dherai 'much, many'. * ḍhēra- ² 'belly' see * ḍhiḍḍha -². * ḍhēra- ³ 'slanting, squinting' see ṭēraka -. * ḍhēlla- ¹ 'lump' see * ḍala -. Addenda: * ḍhēra-¹: S.kcch. ḍherī f. 'heap of thread'; WPah.kṭg. ḍhḕr m. 'heap', J. ḍhēr .
